      "path": "/Users/nick/Documents/crr-2.0.2/README.md",
      "lines": [
        {
          "number": 8,
          "text": "## Release Line Compatibility"
        },
        {
          "number": 9,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "number": 10,
          "text": "This checkout prepares **SDK 2.0.2**, an unpublished failure-evidence safety"
        },
        {
          "number": 11,
          "text": "and readability candidate. Use a matching maintainer-supplied or locally built archive; no new"
        },
        {
          "number": 12,
          "text": "tag, GitHub release or RubyGems publication is implied."
        },
        {
          "number": 13,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "number": 14,
          "text": "| SDK line | Ruby | Cucumber | Candidate source |"
        },
        {
          "number": 15,
          "text": "| --- | --- | --- | --- |"
        },
        {
          "number": 16,
          "text": "| 1.x / **1.3.2** | `>= 3.1` | `>= 9, < 11` | `maintenance/presentation-ledger-1.3.2` |"
        },
        {
          "number": 17,
          "text": "| 2.x / **2.0.2** | `>= 3.3` | `>= 12.0.1`, `~> 12.0` | `codex/failure-redaction-2.0.2` |"
        },
        {
          "number": 18,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "number": 19,
          "text": "Cucumber 11 remains unsupported. Existing published archives and their dated"
        },
        {
          "number": 20,
          "text": "evidence are unchanged. Helm **1.3.1** / ReportPortal **26.0.7** stay independently"
        },
        {
          "number": 21,
          "text": "versioned; this SDK update requires no infrastructure upgrade."
        },
        {
          "number": 22,
          "text": "For Cucumber 12 migration and CI-owned parallel Launches, see the"
        },
        {
          "number": 23,
          "text": "[migration guide](docs/migrating-to-2.0.md). This candidate branch is not an"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "/Users/nick/Documents/crr-2.0.2/docs/best-practices.md",
      "lines": [
        {
          "number": 95,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "number": 96,
          "text": "AppLog prints local date/time, milliseconds and aligned levels, without a"
        },
        {
          "number": 97,
          "text": "source prefix. TTY colors remain automatic; `NO_COLOR=1` disables auto-color."
        },
        {
          "number": 98,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "number": 99,
          "text": "```text"
        },
        {
          "number": 100,
          "text": "2026-10-31 14:32:08.125  INFO   Order submitted"
        },
        {
          "number": 101,
          "text": "2026-10-31 14:32:09.438  WARN   Retrying request"
        },
        {
          "number": 102,
          "text": "2026-10-31 14:32:12.016  ERROR  Payment failed"
        },
        {
          "number": 103,
          "text": "```"
        },
        {
          "number": 104,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "number": 105,
          "text": "The timestamp is terminal-only. Full JSON stays in report evidence and does not"
        },
        {
          "number": 106,
          "text": "flood the summary. This presentation change does not modify RP log timestamps,"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "/Users/nick/Documents/crr-2.0.2/docs/best-practices.md",
      "lines": [
        {
          "number": 123,
          "text": "## API tests: observe real calls, then assert"
        },
        {
          "number": 124,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "number": 125,
          "text": "Instrument the client at the request boundary. Record the actual method, URL,"
        },
        {
          "number": 126,
          "text": "status, relevant headers/body, and elapsed time; return the response unchanged so"
        },
        {
          "number": 127,
          "text": "Steps can assert the business contract. `AppLog.http` performs **no HTTP request**"
        },
        {
          "number": 128,
          "text": "and **no assertion**."
        },
        {
          "number": 129,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "number": 130,
          "text": "The `AppLog.http` preview has a shared **16 KiB / 100 lines** budget across"
        },
        {
          "number": 131,
          "text": "request and response bodies and headers, not a separate allowance per section."
        },
        {
          "number": 132,
          "text": "Redaction runs before preview clipping; clipped content is marked"
        },
        {
          "number": 133,
          "text": "`[preview truncated]`. The RP card spends that budget response-first: title,"
        },
        {
          "number": 134,
          "text": "response subtitle/body, URL, request subtitle/body, request headers, then response"
        },
        {
          "number": 135,
          "text": "headers. Headers show one `name: value` line per value (including repeated names"
        },
        {
          "number": 136,
          "text": "for multi-value headers); content-type subtitles show media type strings, not"
        },
        {
          "number": 137,
          "text": "arrays. Values and credential redaction are preserved within the existing bounds;"
        },
        {
          "number": 138,
          "text": "the compact terminal summary and native Cucumber body format are unchanged."
        },
        {
          "number": 139,
          "text": "Full HTTP bodies are not attached automatically. If a full body is required,"
        },
        {
          "number": 140,
          "text": "save a redacted file and attach it explicitly."
        },
        {
          "number": 141,
          "text": ""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "/Users/nick/Documents/crr-2.0.2/docs/best-practices.md",
      "lines": [
        {
          "number": 229,
          "text": "Pre-redact application-specific fields in the client before logging."
        },
        {
          "number": 230,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "number": 231,
          "text": "For POST/PUT bodies and a real local fixture, copy the"
        },
        {
          "number": 232,
          "text": "[current SDK API client](../examples/current_sdk/helpers/api_client.rb) and read"
        },
        {
          "number": 233,
          "text": "its [runnable example](../examples/current_sdk/README.md). Avoid logging the same"
        },
        {
          "number": 234,
          "text": "full response a second time as JSON unless that extra evidence answers a specific"
        },
        {
          "number": 235,
          "text": "question. For a large required body, store a redacted file and attach it explicitly;"
        },
        {
          "number": 236,
          "text": "the HTTP diagnostic's truncated preview does not automatically attach the full body."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "/Users/nick/Documents/crr-2.0.2/docs/configuration.md",
      "lines": [
        {
          "number": 91,
          "text": "## Presentation and run context"
        },
        {
          "number": 92,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "number": 93,
          "text": "Available in SDK 2.0.2 (introduced in 2.0.1); both options remain opt-in and off by default."
        },
        {
          "number": 94,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "number": 95,
          "text": "| Environment variable | YAML key | Default | Type / use |"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "/Users/nick/Documents/crr-2.0.2/docs/configuration.md",
      "lines": [
        {
          "number": 114,
          "text": "Rich mode never changes native Cucumber messages/HTML, terminal summaries,"
        },
        {
          "number": 115,
          "text": "arbitrary AppLog text, item names/descriptions, or Launch metadata. Rich never"
        },
        {
          "number": 116,
          "text": "adds decoration to ERROR or FATAL: the entire message is byte-identical to plain,"
        },
        {
          "number": 117,
          "text": "including failure cards, failed assertions, failure evidence, ERROR HTTP exchanges"
        },
        {
          "number": 118,
          "text": "and error-level attachment captions. There are no added pills or backtrace folds"
        },
        {
          "number": 119,
          "text": "at these levels. Existing video markup and caller text remain unmodified by the"
        },
        {
          "number": 120,
          "text": "presentation option; it does not strip HTML already present in those messages."
        },
        {
          "number": 121,
          "text": "TRACE through WARN accents add at most 1,024 bytes per message; exceeding that"
        },
        {
          "number": 122,
          "text": "budget retains the plain card. A presentation exception instead restores the"
        },
        {
          "number": 123,
          "text": "original safe fallback text with one nonreflective warning."
        },
        {
          "number": 124,
          "text": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
